<title>ITALY: Olivetti makes 64 bln lire off sale of Acorn stake.</title>
<headline>Olivetti makes 64 bln lire off sale of Acorn stake.</headline>
<dateline>MILAN 1996-09-18</dateline>
<text>
<p>Olivetti said its first-half results showed a 64 billion lire capital gain from the sale by its subsidiary Olivetti Telemedia Spa of 13.25 million shares in British-based PC and software firm Acorn.</p>
<p>Olivetti said in a statement the transaction was being handled by U.S. investment bank Lehman Brothers.</p>
<p>The sum of 64 billion lire was currently deposited with Lehman and would be made over to Olivetti Telemedia in instalments as the shares were placed on the market.</p>
<p>-- Milan newsroom +392-66102321</p>
</text>
